]\r\n    seen = {a.get(\"seq\") for a in before if isinstance(a, dict)}\r\n    return [a for a in after if isinstance(a, dict) and a.get(\"seq\") not in seen]\r\n\r\n\r\ndef lane_approval_refusal(root, base, head, delta=None, reason=None):\r\n    \"\"\"Why a lane's delta may not merge because it performs an APPROVAL ACT no\r\n    verdict was asked to back - the refusal text, or None when it performs no\r\n    act and writes no record. The merge slot words both refusals here: a record\r\n    written with no act behind it, and acts `backed_act_refusal` found unbacked,\r\n192:- **Standing owner acts the loop will not make:** merge-to-main + push for\r\n193:  `dualplan-routing-fix`, `guardrails-fable-method`, `ConcurrencyTrainRewrite`\r\n194:  and this branch (`push = \"human\"`). The held wi508\r\n253:  first-approval and amendment rows'\r\n255:  builds the loop route's act turn); the judging composer's first-approval\r\n377:  pre-push case for a scripts directory found nowhere, and TC-031's method\r\n378:  says every hook drives the adversarial table, where pre-push drives it\r\n382:  reads ON at pre-push; Flow 3 draws the scripts-directory refusal after\r\n448:  staged approval-act, amendment and drafted-row readers and\r\n452:  home is now `kitlib.spine.claims_approval`, is still restated in the\r\n484:  `merge_approval_refusal` keeps a required `trunk` keyword no rule\r\n526:  A7 \"insufficient evidence for approval\" outcome is not mapped onto its\r\n597:  - **WI-987** `P5` — The open-items page lists every stakeholder need and stakeholder owing an approval or a r…\r\n618:  [repo-lock.md](repo-lock.md) · external (not this repo's work): guardrails\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
